// REJECTS: ->subType() is supported only at root level
//
// The bare `->subType(@T){...}` form -- with no property in front of it -- is legal ONLY as
// the immediate child of the tree root. This nests a second one inside the first.
//
// The grammar permits it; the restriction is a walker check, and the message is the whole
// value of this fixture: it is prose, not a token diagnostic, so nothing about it can be
// derived from the .g4. graphfetch-subtype.pure proves both legal placements parse, which
// makes the recursive case look like an obvious generalisation. A generated parser accepts
// it and produces a nested root-level cast the protocol has no representation for.
###Pure
function fixture::neg::nestedRootCast(): meta::pure::metamodel::type::Any[*]
{
   #{
      fixture::neg::Shape {
         area,
         ->subType(@fixture::neg::Circle) {
            radius,
            ->subType(@fixture::neg::Unit) {
               scale
            }
         }
      }
   }#
}
